  <section class="sec-overview">
    <div class="ov-quote">
      <span class="ov-mark">&#8220;</span>
      <p class="ov-lead">Extract content catalogs, metadata, ratings, reviews, watchlists, release schedules, and
        pricing information from streaming platforms and entertainment websites to power competitive intelligence and
        content strategy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="ov-content">
      <h3 class="ov-h2">How Entertainment Businesses Use Extracted Data to Optimize Content Libraries</h3>
      <p class="ov-p">The streaming wars have transformed entertainment. Platforms compete for subscribers with
        exclusive content, regional libraries, pricing strategies, and user experience. Understanding what content
        competitors offer, how they rate, what users are saying, and how pricing changes across regions is essential for
        content acquisition and subscriber retention. We help entertainment businesses, studios, aggregators, and
        analysts extract public data from any streaming platform or entertainment website. Our web extraction pipelines
        are platform agnostic, targeting global OTT services, regional players, and entertainment databases.</p>
      <p class="ov-p">Our entertainment and OTT extraction solutions capture content catalogs including movie titles,
        series titles, episode details, season information, release dates, genres, cast and crew, runtime, age ratings,
        and language availability. We extract metadata such as IMDb scores, Rotten Tomatoes scores, platform specific
        ratings, and user review counts. We capture pricing and subscription data including monthly fees, annual plans,
        tiered pricing like basic, standard, premium, free trial availability, and regional price variations. We also
        extract content availability signals including which titles are leaving soon, new arrivals, and regional content
        library differences. For example, we can extract the full content catalog of a competitor platform in a specific
        country to identify content gaps in your own library. We can extract user rating distributions for original
        content to benchmark performance against industry averages. We can also extract price changes across multiple
        platforms over time to track competitive positioning.</p>
      <p class="ov-p">We build custom entertainment extraction pipelines based on your target platforms, content
        categories, regions, metadata fields, and extraction frequency from daily to monthly. Delivery options include
        content catalog datasets, rating comparison reports, pricing change alerts, release calendar exports, and API
        feeds into your content strategy or competitive intelligence systems. With our extracted data, streaming
        platforms benchmark their libraries against competitors. Content acquisition teams identify high value titles
        missing from their catalog. Pricing analysts track competitor subscription changes in real time. And studios
        measure how their content performs across different OTT services.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="sec-wws">
    <div class="wws-shell">
