      <div class="wws-main">
        <div class="wws-head">
          <span class="wws-count">6 Data Solutions</span>
          <h2 class="wws-h">What We Scrape in<br><em>E-commerce</em></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="wws-topic" id="topic-1">
          <div class="wws-topic-num">01</div>
          <div class="wws-topic-body">
          
            <div class="wws-topic-content">
              <h3 class="wws-topic-t">Catalog &amp; Inventory Monitoring Services</h3>
              <span class="wws-topic-h2">How Businesses Are Using Catalog &amp; Inventory Data to Reduce Costs and
                Capture Demand</span>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Maintaining an accurate, up-to-date product catalog across multiple marketplaces
                and distribution channels is a major operational challenge. Discrepancies in product titles, missing
                attributes, incorrect images, or outdated inventory levels directly lead to lost sales, returns, and
                customer dissatisfaction. We help businesses monitor, validate, and synchronize catalog and inventory
                data at scale using automated data collection pipelines.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Our catalog monitoring solutions extract structured product data   including SKU
                attributes, pricing, availability status, variants, and descriptions   from your own systems and
                competitor platforms. We flag missing fields, duplicate listings, attribute mismatches, and
                non-compliant content before they impact discoverability. On the inventory side, we track stock levels
                across warehouses, retail stores, and marketplace fulfillment centers. Real-time alerts notify you when
                a high-demand SKU falls below safety stock thresholds or when a competitor's product shows sudden
                unavailability, giving you the chance to adjust ordering or capture displaced demand.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">We build custom monitoring pipelines tailored to your product catalog size, channel
                mix (Shopify, Magento, Amazon, eBay, etc.), and monitoring frequency   from hourly to daily. Delivery
                options include anomaly dashboards, automated catalog audit reports, and API webhooks for instant
                inventory alerts. With our data, retailers reduce listing errors by 70%, prevent revenue loss from
                unexpected stockouts, and maintain consistent catalog quality across every sales touchpoint.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="wws-topic" id="topic-2">
          <div class="wws-topic-num">02</div>
          <div class="wws-topic-body">
            
            <div class="wws-topic-content">
              <h3 class="wws-topic-t">Consumer &amp; Market Insights</h3>
              <span class="wws-topic-h2">How Businesses Are Using Consumer Data to Drive Smarter Strategies</span>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Consumer expectations evolve rapidly, and businesses that rely on outdated or
                surface-level insights fall behind. To stay relevant, companies need real-time visibility into what
                customers are searching for, buying, reviewing, and abandoning   across multiple platforms. We help
                businesses collect and analyze consumer-generated data from e-commerce reviews, social media
                conversations, forum discussions, Q&amp;A sections, and product comparison sites. This unstructured
                data, when processed with AI-driven sentiment analysis and trend detection, transforms into actionable
                market intelligence.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Our consumer insights solutions track shifting preferences by product category,
                brand perception over time, feature-level feedback (e.g., &quot;battery life&quot; or &quot;fit&quot;),
                and demographic-based buying patterns. For example, we can identify rising demand for sustainable
                packaging in your category weeks before competitors react, or detect negative sentiment spikes around a
                specific product feature that requires immediate attention. We also benchmark your brand against
                competitors on factors like price perception, customer service ratings, and delivery experience   giving
                you a clear roadmap for improvement.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">We build custom insight pipelines based on your industry, target audience,
                competitor set, and key attributes you care about. Delivery options include sentiment dashboards, trend
                reports, review aggregation with AI summaries, and automated alerts for unusual consumer behavior
                shifts. With our data, marketing teams launch campaigns rooted in real demand, product teams prioritize
                features customers actually want, and executives track brand health with confidence.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="wws-topic" id="topic-3">
          <div class="wws-topic-num">03</div>
          <div class="wws-topic-body">
            
            <div class="wws-topic-content">
              <h3 class="wws-topic-t">Geography &amp; Market expansion</h3>
              <span class="wws-topic-h2">How Businesses Are Using Geographic Data to Expand Smarter and Faster</span>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Expanding into new cities, states, or countries requires more than instinct   it
                requires hard evidence of demand, competition, pricing dynamics, and local consumer behavior. Businesses
                that skip data-driven validation often face mismatched product assortments, unexpected pricing pressure,
                or overlooked local competitors. We help companies collect and analyze location-specific data from
                region-targeted e-commerce sites, local marketplace platforms, distribution partner portals, regional
                pricing indexes, and location-based search trends.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Our market expansion solutions track product availability and pricing by geography,
                competitor presence and share across regions, local promotion patterns, and demand signals from search
                and social data. For example, we can identify that a product category is underserved in a specific metro
                area, determine the optimal entry price point based on local competitor benchmarks, or flag that a
                regional player is aggressively discounting to block new entrants. We also monitor logistics indicators
                  delivery timelines, shipping costs, and stock availability by pin code   to help you assess
                operational feasibility before committing resources.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">We build custom geographic intelligence pipelines based on your target expansion
                zones, product categories, competitor set, and data sources relevant to each region (local marketplaces,
                aggregators, retailer sites). Delivery options include regional heatmaps, market readiness scorecards,
                competitor density reports, and API feeds that integrate with your site selection or store planning
                tools. With our data, expansion teams prioritize high-opportunity regions, reduce costly launch
                mistakes, and enter new markets with confidence backed by local intelligence.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="wws-topic" id="topic-4">
          <div class="wws-topic-num">04</div>
          <div class="wws-topic-body">
            
            <div class="wws-topic-content">
              <h3 class="wws-topic-t">Competitor Price Monitoring Services</h3>
              <span class="wws-topic-h2">How Businesses Are Using Competitor Price Data to Win on Price Without
                Sacrificing Profit</span>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Price is often the fastest-changing variable in e-commerce, yet many businesses
                still monitor competitors manually   leading to slow responses, reactive discounting, and lost sales.
                Real-time competitor price monitoring is no longer optional; it's essential for maintaining search
                ranking, buy box ownership, and customer trust. We help companies collect and analyze structured pricing
                data from competitor websites, marketplaces, distributor portals, and comparison shopping engines at
                scale   from hourly to daily refreshes.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Our competitor price monitoring solutions track list prices, sale prices, bundle
                pricing, per-unit pricing, dynamic surge pricing, shipping costs, and membership-discounted rates. We
                also monitor historical price trends, repricing velocity, and price positioning relative to category
                averages. For example, we can detect that a competitor drops price every Tuesday on a specific SKU,
                identify that your price is 8% above the market leader for a high-volume product, or flag sudden,
                aggressive discounting aimed at stealing your share before a holiday weekend. We also monitor buy box
                ownership and rotation patterns on marketplaces like Amazon to help you optimize for visibility.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">We build custom price monitoring pipelines based on your SKU list, competitor set,
                target geographies, preferred refresh frequency (hourly, daily, weekly), and alert thresholds (e.g.,
                &quot;notify when any competitor price drops below X&quot;). Delivery options include price dashboards
                with trend lines, competitive positioning matrices, automated email/Slack alerts for price changes, and
                API feeds that plug directly into your dynamic repricing engine or ERP system. With our data, e-commerce
                teams respond to price moves in minutes, category managers defend margins with surgical precision, and
                executives gain full visibility into competitive price pressure across every product line.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="wws-topic" id="topic-5">
          <div class="wws-topic-num">05</div>
          <div class="wws-topic-body">
           
            <div class="wws-topic-content">
              <h3 class="wws-topic-t">Rating &amp; Review extraction</h3>
              <span class="wws-topic-h2">How Businesses Are Using Review Data to Improve Products and Customer
                Experience</span>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Customer reviews are one of the richest sources of unfiltered feedback, yet most
                businesses only glance at star ratings or read a handful of recent comments. Buried inside thousands of
                reviews are specific insights   feature requests, recurring complaints, unexpected use cases, and direct
                comparisons with competitors. We help businesses extract and structure review data from e-commerce
                platforms (Amazon, Walmart, Flipkart), app stores (Google Play, Apple App Store), travel sites
                (Tripadvisor, Booking.com), restaurant platforms (Yelp, Zomato), and product forums at scale.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Our rating and review extraction solutions capture reviewer names, star ratings,
                review text, verified purchase badges, helpfulness votes, images/videos attached to reviews, and seller
                responses. We then apply AI-driven sentiment analysis to break down feedback by specific attributes  
                price, quality, durability, customer service, packaging, shipping speed, size/fit, and more. For
                example, we can identify that 68% of 3-star reviews mention &quot;battery life&quot; as the primary
                issue, detect that competitors receive better feedback on &quot;ease of assembly,&quot; or surface that
                customers are using your kitchen gadget for an entirely unintended purpose   revealing a new market
                opportunity.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">We build custom review extraction pipelines based on your products, competitor
                ASINs or product URLs, target platforms, languages, and review attributes you care about. Delivery
                options include sentiment dashboards with attribute breakdowns, review summaries with AI-generated
                insights, competitive comparison matrices, and API feeds that push structured review data into your
                product management or customer insights platform. With our data, product teams fix what customers
                actually complain about, marketing teams highlight strengths backed by real quotes, and customer
                experience teams track satisfaction trends month over month.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="wws-topic" id="topic-6">
          <div class="wws-topic-num">06</div>
          <div class="wws-topic-body">
            
            <div class="wws-topic-content">
              <h3 class="wws-topic-t">Sentiment Analysis from Social Media Services</h3>
              <span class="wws-topic-h2">How Businesses Are Using Social Sentiment Data to Connect with Customers
                Authentically</span>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Social media is where customers speak most freely   celebrating wins, venting
                frustrations, comparing brands, and influencing others. Yet without systematic analysis, these
                conversations remain noise instead of intelligence. Businesses that ignore social sentiment miss early
                warning signs of PR crises, fail to recognize sudden shifts in brand love, and lose opportunities to
                engage when customers are most receptive. We help companies collect and analyze unstructured social data
                from Twitter/X, Reddit, Facebook, Instagram comments, LinkedIn, TikTok captions, YouTube comments, and
                niche forums   transforming casual posts into structured sentiment insights.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">Our sentiment analysis solutions go beyond simple positive/negative classification.
                We detect nuanced emotions   frustration, disappointment, delight, confusion, trust, skepticism   and
                attribute them to specific topics: product features, customer service interactions, delivery
                experiences, pricing reactions, ad campaigns, or competitor comparisons. For example, we can flag that
                negative sentiment around your &quot;checkout process&quot; spiked 400% in 24 hours due to a technical
                glitch, detect that a competitor's new launch is generating &quot;confusion&quot; rather than
                &quot;excitement,&quot; or identify that a specific influencer's mention shifted brand sentiment from
                neutral to highly positive across a target demographic. We also track sentiment velocity (how fast
                sentiment is changing), share of voice by sentiment category, and emotion trends by geography or time of
                day.</p>
              <p class="wws-topic-p">We build custom sentiment pipelines based on your brand name, product lines,
                competitor handles, relevant keywords, target platforms, languages, and demographic filters (region, age
                indicators from profiles). Delivery options include sentiment dashboards with emotion breakdowns,
                real-time alerting for sentiment spikes, trend comparison charts across competitors, and API feeds into
                your social listening or customer experience management systems. With our data, brand teams catch
                reputation fires before they spread, marketing teams measure campaign emotional resonance, and product
                teams hear what customers actually feel   not just what they click.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

